{
  "schema": 1,
  "comment": [
    "The executed evidence behind release/source-lock.json (audit Q42): which runs actually built",
    "the pin set this tree ships, and which branch tip each pin was measured against.",
    "",
    "Why this file exists: `release/source-lock.json` is derived from the tree and proves only that",
    "the pins are CONSISTENT. Nothing in it says a build ever ran against them, and the review that",
    "raised Q42 found exactly that gap - the correspondence lived in prose, and a workflow",
    "DECLARATION was being read as if it were a run. `scripts/ci/check-pin-runs.py` re-reads the",
    "lock out of each recorded commit: a run covers these pins only when the lock at that commit",
    "has the same pin projection as the lock now. Move a pin without recording a new run and the",
    "coverage disappears, offline, on the next push.",
    "",
    "parent_runs: completed runs of THIS repository at a commit whose lock carries the current pin",
    "  set. `Verify` is the build/vet/test gate, `Mobile contract verification` the Apple-tag and",
    "  libbox half, `Android Core ARM64` the cross-compile. A cancelled run is not listed: the",
    "  parent repository cancels superseded runs on the same ref, so a cancelled run is not",
    "  evidence about the pins either way.",
    "child_runs: runs in a child repository that built that client at its pinned revision. Empty",
    "  today, and that is a MEASURED emptiness: on 2026-11-13 `gh run list -R <slug>",
    "  --commit <pin>` was run against all four client repositories and none has a run at the",
    "  pinned revision. The parent runs cover the gitlinks the parent builds; a client's own build",
    "  is additional evidence, not a substitute.",
    "observed_tips: each repository's tracked branch tip, observed on the date given, with the",
    "  relation the freeze's `check` would report. `not-compared` states why a relation could not",
    "  be decided from this checkout, and never stands in for `identical`.",
    "not_covered: pins no parent run in this repository can read, each with the workflow+job that",
    "  does read them. The checker verifies that job still checks submodules out, so a deleted",
    "  compensating gate fails instead of leaving a silently empty section.",
    "",
    "This file records OBSERVATIONS. It is not a second copy of the pins: the pins live in go.mod",
    "and the gitlinks, the lock snapshots them, and `pin`/`head_sha` here only say which run or",
    "observation was about which revision."
  ],
